cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this course, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Snakemake for genomics: a hands-on course"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
authors:
  - family-names: Flores
    given-names: JP
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jpflores-13/snakemake-course"
url: "https://jpflores-13.github.io/snakemake-course"
abstract: >-
  A two-day, hands-on course on writing genomics pipelines with Snakemake 8.
  Learners build a ChIP-seq and DNase-seq pipeline (RegPipe) on public HCT116
  data, then read the lab's production pipelines. Lessons render as web pages
  and slides from one Quarto source, with exercises and public answer keys.
keywords:
  - Snakemake
  - workflow
  - genomics
  - ChIP-seq
  - training
  - Quarto
